176	// Per-window sums are independent: the same event can be safe in an earlier
177	// window while it overflows a later one that earlier events already pushed
178	// to the limit. Window 1000, slide 300: the event at 1000 belongs to
179	// [300,1300) (empty, accepts it fine), [600,1600) and [900,1900) (both
180	// already at MaxInt64 from the event at 1300). The run must fail at that
181	// input line naming [600,1600) — the first window that truly overflows —
182	// not the safe [300,1300). Output closed before the failure is retained and
183	// the watermark after it is never processed.
184	func TestAggregateSlidingSumOverflowNamesOverflowingWindow(t *testing.T) {
